WHY THIS LICENSE, AND WHAT IT DOES NOT FORECLOSE

This is the default position, chosen deliberately and not by omission.

FRIDAY holds the owner's calendar, correspondence, notes, home, and finances.
Reserving all rights keeps every option open while that is true, and it costs
nothing: the copyright holder may relicense this work under any terms at any
time, because they hold all of the copyright in it.

The reverse is not true. Code released under an open license cannot be
un-released. Waiting is free; releasing early is not.

If FRIDAY is ever opened, README.md records the reasoning: AGPL-3.0 is the most
philosophically consistent choice, because it would let others use and modify
her while preventing anyone from building a closed product on work whose
founding documents are about user sovereignty. That decision requires an ADR
and is the owner's alone.

Third-party dependencies remain under their own licenses. See the license
compliance stage of the CI pipeline (docs/01-bible/27-cicd-pipeline.md).
